abstract: >
  The increase of GNSS observations worldwide creates new opportunities for large-scale analysis,
  but also introduces challenges in data holding, retrieval, and quality control. In this frame,
  I introduce an open-source Python package "GRINQ" that automates these steps through a unified
  workflow for retrieving RINEX data across multiple data holdings and computing quality statistics.
  A dedicated mirroring functionality for cloning selected data holdings, enabling users to maintain
  synchronized copies of remote repositories, facilitating large-scale and reproducible analysis
  of GNSS data.


